Minimum complete backend logic for your MVP
If you want your backend to be “done enough” before GUI, these are the must-have operations.

1. Add item
Creates item in DB and logs ITEM_ADDED.
Input

name
category
optional asset tag
quantity
notes

Output

saved item
matching transaction


2. Assign item
Updates current state and logs CHECKED_OUT.
Input

item ID
assigned employee
job site
notes

Business rule
Only assign if:

item exists
item is AVAILABLE
quantity is valid


3. Return item
Updates state to AVAILABLE, clears assignee/job site, logs RETURNED.

4. Retire item
Updates state to RETIRED, logs RETIRED.
Do not hard delete immediately unless you really want that behavior.

5. Search items
Search by:

asset tag
item name
assignedTo
jobSite
category


6. Get all inventory
Needed for GUI table and reports.

7. Get transactions in date range
Needed for your report requirement.

Suggested validation rules
Your backend should enforce these:
For items

name cannot be blank
category cannot be blank
quantity must be greater than 0
assetTag must be unique if provided

For assignment

item must exist
item cannot already be retired
item should usually be available before assignment
jobSite should not be blank when assigning project equipment


